# The front panel's poweroff/reboot buttons (and the halt/restart
# instructions the OS/8 console prints) reach for systemctl. Upstream's
# etc/sudoers.in hardcodes the single user who ran ./configure; the
# package grants the pidp8i group instead, so any operator account added
# to it gets the same capability. Mode 0440 is what sudo(5) requires.
%pidp8i ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl poweroff, /usr/bin/systemctl reboot
